# Additions for the NVIDIA Jetson Nano (Tegra210), composed after
# omarchy-base.packages and omarchy-aarch64.packages.
#
# Deliberately short. The generic aarch64 list already brings zram-generator,
# pipewire-jack and gst-plugin-pipewire, and the Nano needs no proprietary
# NVIDIA userspace on the desktop path: CUDA belongs to the vendor-BSP image,
# not to this one (see docs/decisions/ADR-001-kernel-gpu-strategy.md).
#
# What the Nano does need that aarch64 does not give it:

# Mesa's Tegra/DRI path and the tooling the graphics gate uses. drm_info has no
# aarch64 package in Arch Linux ARM, so the gate uses modetest (libdrm) and
# glxinfo/eglinfo (mesa-utils) instead.
mesa
libdrm
mesa-utils

# The board's Ethernet is a Realtek PCIe NIC (r8169 in the kernel package); the
# userspace side is ethtool for link diagnostics.
ethtool

# Thermal and power observability, since mainline has no nvpmodel.
lm_sensors

# No x86-only applications, no Steam, no dotnet, no proprietary drivers.
